problem_statement:
Load local credential config when invoke local --docker
# Feature Proposal

## Description

<!-- Please use https://forum.serverless.com, StackOverflow or other forums for Q&A -->
<!-- Please answer ALL the question below. Otherwise we probably have to close the issue due to missing information -->

1. What is the use case that should be solved. The more detail you describe this in the easier it is to understand for us.

If there is the proper credential setting in local, the handler which access to AWS service like the following should work when `invoke local --docker`.

```
"use strict";

const AWS = require("aws-sdk");

module.exports.hello = async event => {
  const ssm = new AWS.SSM();
  console.log(await ssm.getParameter({ Name: "test" }).promise());
};
```

`invoke local` (without `--docker`) and [sam local invoke](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/serverless-application-model/latest/developerguide/sam-cli-command-reference-sam-local-invoke.html) support this, but `invoke local --docker` doesn't.

