problem_statement:
Throw a custom exception when a validator has errors
At the moment, the only way to throw a custom exception when a validator has errors is using an `if`:
```java
app.get("/users/{id}", ctx -> { 
    Validator<Long> id = ctx.pathParamAsClass("id", Long.class);
    if (id.errors().isEmpty()) {
      throw new UserNotFoundException(id.errors());
    }
    ctx.json(usersRepository.getById(id.get()));
})
app.exception(UserNotFoundException.class, (e, ctx) -> ctx.render("user-not-found.peb", e.getModel()));
```
I think it would be nice to have a `getOrThrow()` method, similar to [`orElseThrow()` from `Optional<T>`](https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/17/docs/api//java.base/java/util/Optional.html#orElseThrow(java.util.function.Supplier)). The custom exception could receive the validation `errors()` via parameter and retreive relevant information from there:

```java
app.get("/users/{id}", ctx -> { 
    Long id = ctx.pathParamAsClass("id", Long.class)
        .getOrThrow(errors -> new UserNotFoundException(errors));
    ctx.json(usersRepository.getById(id));
})
app.exception(UserNotFoundException.class, (e, ctx) -> ctx.render("user-not-found.peb", e.getModel()));
```

I could add this feature if you'd like.

