problem_statement:
Mysterious overhead being added between journey start/stop and step start/stop
The `monitor.duration` in the heartbeat summary is calculated based purely on the differences of times between the `journey/start` and `journey/end` events. See https://github.com/elastic/beats/blob/master/x-pack/heartbeat/monitors/browser/synthexec/enrich.go#L167 for the implementation.

In the real world we extra time accounted for between journey start/stop and step start/end events. We should figure out why.

Running a simple journey locally I see:

```
# elastic-synthetics . --match "check if title is present" --reporter json --screenshots off | jq '{t: .type, ts: ."@timestamp"}'
{
  "t": "synthetics/metadata",
  "ts": 1636138571717791.8 // T=-0.282s
}
{
  "t": "journey/start",
  "ts": 1636138572000137.5 // T=0s
}
{
  "t": "step/end",
  "ts": 1636138572231909.8 // T=0.23s
}
{
  "t": "step/end",
  "ts": 1636138572265338.5 // T=0.26s
}
{
  "t": "journey/end",
  "ts": 1636138572265777.2 // T=0.265s
}
```

So, I'm seeing a total of `0.235s` time added as overhead.

