[sitemaps] Allow to normalize URLs in sitemaps
Url strings  without protocol will produce MalformedURLException. Add protocol to url string if it missing and not strict mode.
Example: http://www.clasohlson.com/sitemap.xml

```
private void maybeAddSiteMap() {
        if (loc == null) {
            return;
        }
        String locUrlString = stripAllBlank(loc);
        //url string without protocol will produce MalformedURLException 
        if (!isStrict()) { //maybe add new flag that user can specify if we should auto assign protocol 
            if (!locUrlString.isEmpty() && !locUrlString.contains("://")) { // simple check if we have "://" in string, or maybe regex that handles ALL protocols what is hard [http, https, ftp, ssl...]
                locUrlString = sitemap.getUrl().getProtocol() + "://" + locUrlString; // get protocol from the sitemap
            }
