problem_statement:
Relative redirect_uri not accepted by Okta
I'm trying to get APIFlask's swagger page to work with Okta auth and running into an issue. When I click the authorize button in the swagger ui I'm taken to a url like the following:
`https://my-domain.okta.com/oauth2/default/v1/authorize?response_type=token&client_id=123abc&redirect_uri=%2Flogin%2Fcallback`

The redirect_uri is a relative path to the route but okta requires a full url. I'm not sure if other authentication services accept relative routes, perhaps this is an incompatibility rather than a bug.

**Expected Behavior**:
Clicking on the authorize button from the swagger UI should take me to `https://my-domain.okta.com/oauth2/default/v1/authorize?response_type=token&client_id=123abc&redirect_uri=https%3A%2F%2F%2Fmy-domain.com%2Flogin%2Fcallback`

**Replicate:**
Here's my config:
```
    app = APIFlask(
        "My-App",
        docs_oauth2_redirect_path="/login/callback",
        docs_ui="swagger-ui",
    )
    oauth2 = {
        "type": "oauth2",
        "flows": {
            "implicit": {
                "authorizationUrl": "https://my-domain.okta.com/oauth2/default/v1/authorize",
                "scopes": {},
            }
        },
    }
    security_schemes = {
        "oauth2": oauth2,
    }
    app.security_schemes = security_schemes
    app.config["SWAGGER_UI_OAUTH_CONFIG"] = {
        "clientId": "123abc",
        "scopes": "openid",
        "additionalQueryStringParams": {
            "nonce": "123",
        },
    }
    app.config["SERVERS"] = [
        {"name": "Prod", "url": "https://my-domain.com"},
        {"name": "Dev", "url": "https://dev.my-domain.com"},
    ]
    app.config["SWAGGER_UI_OAUTH_REDIRECT_DECORATORS"] = [<my_custom_authenticate_method>]
```


Environment:
- Python version: 3.10.6
- Flask version: 2.2.2
- APIFlask version: 2.2.0

