problem_statement:
Move default port configuration to `JavalinConfig`
By default, Javalin starts on port ::8080 and there's no option to configure this behavior within the configuration scope.

https://github.com/javalin/javalin/blob/4a6240bf57c161d8f6dc0bea5e2edf20aa05da42/javalin/src/main/java/io/javalin/Javalin.java#L121-L129

It'd be nice, if we could move this property to cfg:

```kotlin
val app = Javalin
  .create(cfg -> {
    cfg.defaultPort = 1234;
  })
  .start();
```

Effectively, we could even simplify this to:

```kotlin
// default ::8080
val app = Javalin.start()

// custom port/other cfg properties
val app = Javalin.start(cfg -> {
  cfg.defaultPort = 1234;
})
```

**Edit**
Same thing with hostname.

